Rebuttal to Argument Against Measure D
Don’t be misled by false claims and misinformation. Why would
Ranked Choice Voting (RCV) be used by 17 million voters in cities across
California and the US if it was so expensive to implement? RCV will give
Irvine voters more choice, stronger local representation, and true
majority rule.
Vote YES on Measure D because:
• Exaggerated Cost Claims: Implementation costs are minimal —
no other city adopting Ranked Choice Voting has spent that much
money.
• Strict Cost Limits: Measure D includes a hard spending limit
of 0.23% of the city budget, fully protecting taxpayers. RCV
will only be used if the cost is less than 0.23% of the budget…It’s
that simple.
• Sensible Timeline: Implementation is scheduled after
January 1, 2028, giving election officials ample time to certify
equipment and conduct thorough voter education.
• Majority Should Rule: In Irvine, unpopular candidates can win
with just a small fraction of the vote. RCV solves this problem.
With RCV, candidates need to earn over 50% popular support
to win.
• Instantaneous Results: RCV will not cause additional delays;
once ballots are collected, the voting equipment counts in an
eyeblink.
• Simple as 1-2-3: Just rank your favorite candidates in order
of preference. If your top choice is eliminated, your vote
automatically counts for your next choice, making sure your vote
is never wasted.
Ranked Choice Voting will support a stronger, more representative local
government and put power back in the hands of Irvine voters, where it
belongs.
VOTE YES on Measure D.
